        "role": "assistant",
        "phase": "commentary",
        "text_utf8": "Agreed. The harness-specific final prose is not a stable product contract, so requiring byte-exact terminal prose is the wrong invariant.\n\nThe stable contract should be:\n\n- native Goal must activate and complete;\n- the model must emit one schema-valid typed result somewhere in the bounded task lifecycle;\n- the host deterministically extracts, validates, and canonicalizes that result;\n- conflicting multiple results fail;\n- surrounding prose and harness-specific final wording are ignored.\n\nThat keeps semantics, authority, and lifecycle strict while making the output portable to PuppetMaster’s eventual native runtime. I’ll pivot the qualification to a fresh normalized-output denominator; no old failure gets retro-credit.",
